### Scenario 1 - catalog price for a GOLD customer (1) vs a STANDARD one (3)
### Seed: customer 1 = GOLD, 2 = SILVER, 3 = STANDARD (tiers are derived from the order history)

@catalog = http://localhost:8081
@customer = http://localhost:8082

### Customer 1 profile: tier GOLD (computed from 12-month revenue, cached 10 min)
GET {{customer}}/customers/1

### Customer 3 profile: tier STANDARD
GET {{customer}}/customers/3

### Wireless Mouse, GOLD: customerPrice = 29.90 - 10% = 26.91
GET {{catalog}}/products/ELC-3001?customerId=1

### Wireless Mouse, SILVER: customerPrice = 28.40 (5% discount, rounded on the discount amount)
GET {{catalog}}/products/ELC-3001?customerId=2

### Wireless Mouse, STANDARD: customerPrice = 29.90
GET {{catalog}}/products/ELC-3001?customerId=3

### Product on sale (ELC-3004): the sale price wins, no tier discount -> 149.00 for everybody
GET {{catalog}}/products/ELC-3004?customerId=1

### Filtered list: books under 40 EUR that are available
GET {{catalog}}/products?category=BOOKS&maxPrice=40&available=true
